 "summary": "Used when dense smoke or fumes become the greatest threat. Keep the air flowing (CAB FANS OFF and PACK FLOW HI, unless there are fuel vapours), raise the landing elevation to 10 000 ft / MEA-MORA and start a descent to FL 100 / MEA-MORA. Then go back to the SMOKE / FUMES / AVNCS SMOKE procedure during the descent. At FL 100 the cabin is depressurised and RAM AIR is used. If smoke persists: max 200 kt, cockpit door open, and open the PM sliding window.",
