 "status": null,
 "background": [
  {
   "text": "The most effective means of smoke/fumes removal is ram air: descend to FL 100 or MEA-MORA while the cabin altitude is raised to 10 000 ft or MEA-MORA. The higher cabin altitude also reduces, at least temporarily, the smoke/fumes concentration.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "PRO-ABN-SMOKE",
     "page": "P 28/50",
     "pdf": 3985
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "With fuel vapours, CAB FANS ON: recirculated air ventilates the air mixer bay and other fuselage areas, preventing fuel vapour accumulation and the risk of explosion; passenger health is not affected.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "PRO-ABN-SMOKE",
     "page": "P 28/50",
     "pdf": 3985
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Without fuel vapours, CAB FANS OFF prevents smoke/fumes from entering the cockpit and cabin; PACK FLOW HI gives maximum airflow. Do not shut down the packs or reduce ventilation to smother the fire. Do not deploy oxygen masks if fire is suspected in the cabin.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "PRO-ABN-SMOKE",
     "page": "P 28/50",
     "pdf": 3985
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In ELEC EMER CONFIG, APU MASTER ON closes the battery contactors for a maximum of 3 min, so the crew can manually control the outflow valve powered by the DC BAT BUS.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "PRO-ABN-SMOKE",
     "page": "P 29/50",
     "pdf": 3986
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "If there is smoke/fumes in the cockpit, open the cockpit window to evacuate it. Due to the increased noise level, pay particular attention to visual warnings.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "PRO-ABN-SMOKE",
     "page": "P 29/50",
     "pdf": 3986
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "technique": [
  {
   "text": "The [QRH] SMOKE / FUMES / AVNCS SMOKE procedure: diversion anticipated (LAND ASAP), immediate actions, then — if the source is not immediately isolated — diversion and descent, origin identification and fighting. Boxed items (REMOVAL OF SMOKE / FUMES, ELEC EMER CONFIG, immediate landing) may be applied at any time, but not before the immediate actions.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-SMOKE",
     "page": "P 3/10",
     "pdf": 500
    },
